  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1208 AM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nA strong upper-level trough will continue progressing off to the \neast, with a ridge building in behind it. Temperatures look to stay \nquite cool Friday with high temperatures in the mid 50s across the \ncombined Panhandles. Friday night's low temperatures may approach \nfreezing temperatures and may even dip into the upper 20s in the \nnorthern and northwestern Panhandles, frost and freeze products may \nbe needed. As the ridge builds in and a cutoff low moves over the \nSouthwest US, we are expecting temperatures to gradually warm up \nthrough the weekend and into next week.  \n\nThe upper-level ridge looks to stick with us through the next week, \nthough some operational models want to initialize a shortwave trough \nover Colorado putting us in a favorable location Sunday night and \nMonday for some precipitation. However, the other models do not \nagree with this solution, and a lot of variables remain unsettled. \nWe will be watching this over the next few days and adjust the \nforecast as needed. \n\nMidweek next week, a deep trough off the Pacific Coast will begin to \nmove over the Western US and move east. Exact impacts are not known \nat this time, however, it is another weather system we will watch \nover the several days to see how it progresses. \n\nAbdullayev/Vanden Bosch",
